{
  "name": "Forms · Events Poller",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Forms · Events Poller (Raw Log → n8n)\nEvery minute: `n8n_events(actor, { afterEventId | afterTs, limit })` through the Router → one item per new event → routed by `source`.\nEvent item: `{ eventId, ts, kind, source, workflowId, actor, payload, internalEmployeeId, formId }`.\n\n**Kinds:** `submit` = the form payload as posted (first line of every submit handler; workflowId is empty for creates). `result` = post-write event carrying the final ids — emitted today for **submitInitialRequest** (`workflowId, formId, internalEmployeeId, …`) and **submitEmployeeIDSetup**. The Initial Request / ID Setup outputs below fire on `kind:'result'` so George gets the ids; the `submit` twins land in *Other*.\n**Sources seen today:** submitInitialRequest, submitEmployeeIDSetup, submitHRVerification, submitITSetup, submitITConfirmation, submitSpecialistForm, submitEquipmentRequest, submitTerminationRequest, submitTerminationApproval, submitPositionChangeRequest, submitPositionChangeApproval.\n**Task events** (`task.created` / `task.closed`) are **emitted by Forms since 2026-09-17** (`Services/ActionItemService.js` → `rawLogEvent_('task.created'|'task.closed')`, payload: taskId, workflowId, category, formType, assignedTo/closedBy) — the JR trigger can move from the Gmail regex to `task.created {formType:'jr_title'}` once the TEST tier proves the poller.\n\nCursor = workflow static data (`afterEventId`, `afterTs`, `seen[]`). `pruned:true` → cursor reset to `afterTs = now-1d`. Static data only persists for **active-workflow** executions; a manual run always reads the last 24 h. Replace `<<ROUTER_WORKFLOW_ID>>` before activating. Attach the *Error Notifications - Global Handler* as the error workflow.",
        "width": 1180,
        "height": 470,
        "color": 4
      },
